      "camp_700_claim": "In Swiss Jass / Augenspiele tradition, counters are internal trick-pile weights. Phoenix (-25) is an internal penalty deduction against positive points won, not an active transfer liability. It cannot create a 'trick point overdraft' below 0.",
      "rebuttal": "This is external genre extrapolation that directly contradicts the literal rule text. Urs Hostettler did not write a floor or offset condition. The rule states: 'Each partnership adds together the values of the cards in the tricks it has won... Phoenix: minus 25 points.' If a pile contains only the Phoenix, its sum is literally -25."
